  "correction_rules": [
    "Model tends to overestimate prices in the short term (1-3 days) after spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or slightly positive.",
    "Underestimates prices during early recovery phases after sharp declines, particularly when sentiment remains flat or negative.",
    "Overreacts to recent high sentiment (e.g., 0.25) by pushing forecasts upward, leading to overshoots — apply downward adjustment by 5-10% in such cases.",
    "Mean reversion is evident in 30-day forecasts: model often fails to correct for recent over- or under-estimations, especially when sentiment is stable.",
    "Lag error: model consistently forecasts 1-2 days too late for price reversals — adjust forecast horizon by adding 1-2 days of lagged sentiment data for better alignment.",
    "When sentiment is consistently 0.00, model should not assume upward momentum — apply a conservative baseline correction to avoid over-optimism."
  ]
}
